API.md §5.7: two numbered families of a record on the wire that share the numbers 0 to n-1 are two
numbered columns: one finding at the first field, naming the first and last field and the two
stems, which become the templates of one @json(pairs:) list.
-- project.canon --
project acme {
  canon: "0.1"
}
-- m/m.canon --
package m

record Modifier {
  kind0: Int
  amount0: Int
  kind1: Int
  amount1: Int
  note: String = ""
}

let mods: table Modifier = load("mods.json")
-- m/mods.json --
{
  "a": { "kind0": 1, "amount0": 2, "kind1": 3, "amount1": 4, "note": "x" }
}
-- findings.txt --
warning[W0002]  m/m.canon:4:3
  fields kind0 to amount1 are two numbered columns: one list with @json(pairs: ["kind{i}", "amount{i}"]) keeps the wire

0 errors, 1 warning in 1 package (…)
